  "title": "Ben Simmons Trade Proposal Revealed By Popular NBA Analyst",
  "htmlContent": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":512092,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/GettyImages-1324608641-683x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-512092\"/><figcaption>(Photo by Tim Nwachukwu/Getty Images)</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>On Sunday evening, the Atlanta Hawks eliminated the Philadephia 76ers in game seven on the road. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Sixers head coach Doc Rivers if Ben Simmon could be the starting point guard of a championship team. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>\"I don't know the answer to that,\" Rivers said. <gwmw style=\"display:none;\"><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/statmuse/status/1406803628891934723?s=20\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"twitter\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://twitter.com/statmuse/status/1406803628891934723?s=20\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Simmons was not only a horrible offense against the Hawks; he was invisible. He might as well not have been out there. And during some critical minutes throughout the fourth quarter of game seven, he was not on the floor.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Simmons also went 25-for-73 [34.2%] of the free-throw line during the playoffs. It's the worst free-throw percentage in a single playoffs (minimum 70 attempts) in NBA history.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/statmuse/status/1406812220277755912?s=20\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"twitter\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://twitter.com/statmuse/status/1406812220277755912?s=20\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Rivers, on Ben Simmons' free-throws and lack of aggressiveness:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>\"I still believe in him, but we have work to do. We're gonna have to get in the gym, put a lot of work in and go for it, \" <a href=\"https://twitter.com/DerekBodnerNBA/status/1406806901808058369?s=20\">according to Derek Bodner</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Well, according to Bally Sports' Brandon 'Scoop B' Robinson, Simmon could be in Portland next season. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>\"Portland Trail Blazers could be a team who inquires about Ben Simmons IF the Philadelphia 76ers All Star is made available this summer,\" <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ScoopB/status/1406821188505067520?s=20\">tweeted Robinson</a>.<gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/ScoopB/status/1406821188505067520?s=20\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"twitter\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://twitter.com/ScoopB/status/1406821188505067520?s=20\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>He would follow up that tweet by sharing that Minnesota and Denver could also be suitors for Simmons services. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>\"Minnesota Timberwolves and Denver Nuggets would also make logical sense IF Ben Simmons were made available this off-season. Exciting times ahead,\" <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ScoopB/status/1406821829201776641?s=20\">tweeted Robinson</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Atlanta beat the Sixers 103 to 96 to advance to the Eastern Conference Final for the first time since 2015 to play the Milwaukee Bucks. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
